---
/**
 * THE HOME PAGE, IN EVERY LANGUAGE: the chrome, the two sections, and
 * the floor.
 *
 *   PageBackdrop   the ground. First in the slot and OUTSIDE <main>: one
 *                  fixed layer behind the header, the section and the
 *                  footer alike, not content of any of them.
 *   Header         white, sticky, shadowed.
 *   SideNav        the drawer the header's hamburger opens.
 *   HeroMethod     the greeting and the method, from <locale>/home.md.
 *   Programs       the two tracks. It follows HeroMethod for the reason
 *                  HeroMethod ends without a CTA of its own: the section
 *                  closes on its takeaway line, and the first action a
 *                  visitor is offered is the one in Programs. That
 *                  hand-off is the whole argument for the combined hero,
 *                  and it only exists when the two are adjacent.
 *   Footer         white and shadowed like the header: the two bars
 *                  bracket the document.
 *
 * IT'S A DYNAMIC ROUTE NOW, and that's the only thing this file gained
 * when Russian arrived. `[...locale]` is a rest param set to `undefined`
 * for Hebrew and `'ru'` for Russian, so the two home pages come out as
 * `/` and `/ru` from one file — see [navpage].astro for why the rest
 * param rather than a plain segment. Nothing below branches on the
 * language: every component reads `Astro.currentLocale` for itself.
 *
 * THE TITLE AND DESCRIPTION COME FROM THE CONTENT, not from literals
 * here as they used to. They have to exist in two languages, and
 * <locale>/home.md is already where the rest of this page's words live
 * — a second copy in this file is a second thing to translate and a
 * second thing to forget.
 *
 * NO OTHER SECTIONS. The nav's six destinations are pages of their own
 * ([navpage].astro), not anchors on this one, so nothing here scrolls.
 *
 * WHICH LEAVES `#contact` DANGLING. Programs' closing band and the
 * footer's WhatsApp icon resolve there, because `whatsappHref()` falls
 * back to the anchor while `contact.phone` is a TODO in site.ts. There
 * is no contact section on the page, so both are inert. A number in
 * site.ts fixes them without touching a component — and the clinic's
 * Russian «Контакты и запись» document supplies one.
 *
 * BaseLayout rather than a site-wide shell: the chrome is three
 * components in a known order, and the one page that varies it (the
 * prose pages put ProsePage between them) would have had to opt out of
 * the shell anyway.
 */
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';

import Footer from '../../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/layout/Header.astro';
import PageBackdrop from '../../components/layout/PageBackdrop.astro';
import SideNav from '../../components/layout/SideNav.astro';
import HeroMethod from '../../components/sections/HeroMethod.astro';
import Programs from '../../components/sections/Programs.astro';
import { currentLocale, defaultLocale, locales } from '../../data/i18n';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return locales.map((locale) => ({
    params: { locale: locale === defaultLocale ? undefined : locale },
  }));
}

const locale = currentLocale(Astro);

/* `nav: false`, so [navpage].astro gives this copy no route of its own —
   this file is its route, and HeroMethod is what renders it. */
const home = await getEntry('pages', `${locale}/home`);
if (!home) {
  throw new Error(`The home page needs src/content/pages/${locale}/home.md.`);
}
---

<BaseLayout title={home.data.title} description={home.data.description}>
  <PageBackdrop />
  <Header />
  <SideNav />

  <main id="main">
    <HeroMethod />
    <Programs />
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
